The values of dipole moments of methyl halides:

\begin{aligned}
& $\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{~F}-$1.51 $\mathrm{D}$ ; $\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{Cl}-$1.56 $\mathrm{D}$ ; \\
& $\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{Br}-$1.4 $\mathrm{D}$ ; $\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{I}-$1.29 $\mathrm{D}$ \\
& \therefore \quad $\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{Cl}$>$\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{~F}$>$\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{Br}$>$\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{I}$ .
\end{aligned}
